          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>The Impact on Open Source Software</strong><br>\nAlthough Stallman is not as closely associated with the term \"open source,\" his work with the GNU Project and the GPL has had a significant impact on the open-source software movement. The open-source initiative, which began in 1998, was influenced by the principles and practices that Stallman had been promoting for years.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Recognition and Awards</strong><br>\nThroughout his career, Stallman has received various awards and recognitions for his contributions to the field of computing. These include the Grace Murray Hopper Award from the Association for Computing Machinery (ACM) and a fellowship at the MacArthur Foundation, recognizing his pioneering work in promoting free software.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Later Years and Continuing Influence</strong><br>\nIn recent years, Richard Stallman continues to be an active voice in the free software community. Despite controversies and debates surrounding his views and methods, his influence on the world of software development and digital rights remains substantial. Stallman's work continues to inspire and challenge the way people think about software freedom and access.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
